        <activityName xml:lang="en">Portland calcareous cement, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Portland calcareous cement, at plant
Part of total Swiss cement production: 50%. Composition: gypsum 5%, additional milling substances 16%, clinker 79%;
Synonyms: Zement, Portlandzement, cement, portland cement, CEM II A-L 32.5; 
UUID: 2ffd8a81-33cb-36a8-8013-ab632d0363af
includes the manufacturing processes mixing and grinding, internal processes (transport, etc.) and infrastructure (specific machines and plant). No administration and no packing is included. Special inputs: additional milling substances for example dust from the cement rotary kiln, fly ash, silica dust, limestone; these are not balanced as they are wastes to which no burdens are allocated within ecoinvent.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Typical technology for Swiss production
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 1344151.5 t/a
Sampling: most data measured by all Swiss plants (8 plants) 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2ffd8a81-33cb-36a8-8013-ab632d0363af.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
